# Dependencies and build output.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test output. Not the fixtures — see the note at the bottom, those are load-bearing.
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Working directories. Every top-level folder prefixed with an underscore is
# local source material or scratch, never part of the app and never served:
#
#   _sounds/   95MB of master WAVs. The game fetches the conditioned .ogg and
#              .opus in `public/audio/`; these are what you re-cut from.
#   _models/   Raw kit downloads. The four vehicles the game loads live in
#              `public/models/`, and the CC0 licence is at `docs/`.
#   _art/      Masters and working files, plus the `npm run refsheet` renders,
#              which rebuild in ten seconds and go stale the moment the paint
#              changes — a stale committed copy is worse than none.
#
# The pattern is the rule, so a new `_whatever/` is ignored without an edit.
# Anything that has to survive a clone goes in `public/`, `docs/` or `src/`.
/_*/

# Local tooling state. Editor config and agent settings, not application code.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Secrets. Nothing here today and it stays that way.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# OS junk.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Deploy scratch, for when this goes to a subdomain.
.vercel
.netlify

# NOT ignored, deliberately, because each one looks disposable and is not:
#
#   tests/e2e/fixtures/*.png   The visual-regression baseline. A missing baseline
#                              does not fail the test — the test records a new one
#                              and goes GREEN, so ignoring this turns a real guard
#                              into a decoration on every fresh clone.
#   tests/**/fixtures/*.json   Replay fixtures. They are generated by
#                              `npm run record`, and they are what assert that the
#                              sim is deterministic.
#   docs/art/cover.png         The README cover image.
#   public/**                  Everything the browser fetches at runtime.
#   tracker/                   Small, and it is the honest record of what is and
#                              is not built.
